see "../src/gen_basics.vox".

(The ledger's file leaves, batch B3 - docs/ledger/files.md rows FIL-57,
 FIL-58, FIL-59, FIL-60, FIL-61, FIL-62, FIL-63, FIL-89, FIL-100,
 FIL-102 - the Seek family (emitted by no leaf anywhere before this
 batch) plus the two resource-safety rows.

 Same shape as 380_gen_files_b.vox/381_gen_files_b2.vox: each leaf
 called directly off a pinned rng seed, its emitted source printed in
 full as the golden, rendered both at the true top level (nested false)
 and inside a block (nested true).)
Set gen_scratch_flag to "'the workspace'".
Set gen_does_file_io to true.

Print "--- FIL-58, FIL-59, FIL-60, FIL-62: seek by byte, both keywords, both directions ---".
'rng seed' of 11.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek by byte' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 11.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek by byte' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- FIL-57, FIL-61, FIL-102, FIL-63 (line past EOF): seek by line ---".
'rng seed' of 6.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek by line' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- the same leaf, nested ---".
'rng seed' of 6.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek by line' of "  " and true.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- FIL-63 (position below 1, invalid descriptor): seek invalid targets ---".
'rng seed' of 3.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek invalid targets' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- FIL-100: closing an already-closed handle ---".
'rng seed' of 4.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file double close' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

Print "--- FIL-89: a forgotten Close still reaches disk ---".
'rng seed' of 2.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file forgotten close' of "" and false.
Print 'gen text'.

(A program that never committed to file I/O was never given a path, so
 every leaf above must stand aside for the plain-print leaf instead of
 inventing one - the same guarantee 381_gen_files_b2.vox already checks
 for batch B2's own leaves.)
Print "--- every leaf above with no file I/O committed ---".
Set gen_does_file_io to false.
'rng seed' of 11.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek by byte' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 6.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek by line' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 3.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file seek invalid targets' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 4.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file double close' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 2.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file forgotten close' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
Set gen_does_file_io to true.
